# World 2's gameplay slice (SPEC 4.4, 11 "World 2's gameplay"): mission 4, Reef Run, played.
# Ctrl+L, W, 4 starts it behind its card (the strip map: islands, barracks, pads, hangar).
# - water is a soft stop with a splash: fly out over the sea west of the base island and
#   descend: the skids stop at the surface, a splash shows, nothing is lost;
# - a pad: land on island 4's (x 3312, 64 px wide on normal); the pad guide is drawn;
# - the island barracks opens to the cannon from the pad (two shots, 192 px away), its 16
#   people walk to the chopper and board, and fly home to the base island's pad: 16 saved.
# No dropped frames, worst <= 85 % (the world's budget, tests/world2.agk).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 700
# skill 2: mission 4's patrol boat is armed from skill 3 (Paul, 2026-11-14)
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x02
wait 5
wait 30
screenshot card
press fire 2
wait 50
screenshot base
press up 30
press left 100
wait 40
press down 90
wait 20
screenshot splash
press up 20
press left 150
wait 40
press down 120
wait 60
screenshot pad
expect-color pad 176 210 0xFC3 # (skill 2: the pad is 80 px wide, not skill 3's 64)
press fire 1
wait 30
press fire 1
wait-serial "barracks open=3" 100
wait-serial "aboard=16" 900
screenshot boarded
press up 30
press right 250
wait 60
press down 100
wait-serial "saved=16" 500
screenshot saved
expect-serial "AGK world=2 mission=4"
expect-serial "AGK splash"
expect-serial "landed x=33\d\d"
expect-serial "landed x=41\d\d"
expect-no-serial "chopper lost|ERR|missing"
# the base ocean pens (SPEC 11): the two copper lists never show water steps more than 1 apart, or the water flickers
# (the old policy let a list that skipped a busy picture fall up to 14 steps behind the other: the pens jumped 9 levels)
expect-no-serial "bspread=([2-9]|[1-9][0-9])"
expect-serial "bspread=1"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 85
expect-min-chip-free 96
